-- title:
--   Integrability of finite maximal moments for bounded box-supported data
-- statement:
--   For functions $B,C$ on the plane and a kernel $K$, the cyclic kernel output is $\int_{\mathbb R}B(z_2,c)\,C(c,z_1)\,K(z_1+z_2+c)\,dc$, and the hard kernel is $H_{r,R}(t)=\mathbf 1_{r<|t|\le R}/t$. Let $B,C$ be measurable, bounded by $C_B,C_C$ and supported in $[-M,M]^2$, and let $K_k$ be finitely many measurable kernels bounded by $L$. Then
--   $$
--   z\longmapsto\max_k\bigl|\mathrm{output}(B,C,K_k)(z)\bigr|^{3/2}
--   $$
--   is integrable on $\mathbb R^2$.
--
--   Bounded compactly supported data give finite maximal moments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/CyclicMeasurable.lean#L54-L75

